    "https://hr.wwu.edu/vacancy-support": {
      "title": "If an employee is leaving their position",
      "description": "Vacancy Support | Human Resources | Western Washington University Skip to Content Home Jobs Employee Resources New Employees New Faculty Onboarding Orientation Relocation Resources Student Employment Current Employees Benefits, Disability and Leaves Compensation Employee Perks Employee Recognition Employee Support Resources Employment Verifications Faculty Info Hub HR Announcements Inclement Weather and Suspended Operations Leaving Western Payroll Professional Development/Required Trainings Professional Staff Organization Professional Staff Leave Guidelines Pro-Staff PageUp Performance Evaluation Guides Public Service Loan Forgiveness (PSLF) Program Required Workplace Posters State Employee Whistleblower Act Student Employment Telework WA State Address Confidentiality Program Upcoming HR Trainings Unions & Bargained Agreements Classified Unions Faculty Union WAWU Union Overtime Eligible Resources Suspended Operations Work Tools Banner Resources FAST Resources PageUp Resources Policies & Forms Forms HR and Administrative Forms Web Forms Finder Policies Ethics Policies HR policies Supervisor and Hiring Resources Supervisors Deadlines Calendar HR Trainings for Supervisors Performance Evaluations Pro-staff Pageup Performance Evaluation Guides Student Employment Supervisor Change Form Supervisor QuickStart Training Vacancy Support Volunteer Registration Hiring Hiring Overview Recruitment Toolkit Interviewing Toolkit Onboarding Information for Supervisors Contact Contact Directory Organization Chart for Human Resources Vacancy Support If an employee is leaving their position In an effort to provide supervisors and departments with a smooth transition when they have an employee leaving a position (transferring to another position within WWU), resigning (Leaving WWU), or retiring, Human Resources has put together the following checklist to keep the process as simple as possible. Steps to take once you receive notice from an employee Obtain resignation or retirement letter from the employee Create and route a Personnel Action Form (PA) to end the employee’s position Attach a copy of the resignation letter to the PA Send original resignation letter to MS 9054 for the employee’s personnel file Review the Leaving Western webpage for next steps. Recommend that employee meet with the Benefits Staff if they have any questions or concerns about their transition Is this employee a Payroll Approver?  If so, run NWRAPPR in Banner to see who they are set up to approve time sheets for and complete a Request to Change Payroll Approver form to assign a new Payroll Approver Encourage your employee to complete the Job Documentation Tool to support your department during the personnel transition. Is this employee leaving Western? If so, we have helpful information on our website to help in their transition. Once the term PA has been processed in HR, the employee will be invited to complete our confidential Exit Interview Questionnaire. For additional information, please feel free to contact Human Resources at ext. 3774. Steps to prepare for position vacancy/recruitment After you have received notice from your employee Complete Position Description Form: Classified Professional Staff Submit to hr.comp@wwu.edu for review Once you have approval, begin the recruitment process Throughout the transition process, it is important to keep in mind that if you are considering combining positions or reorganizing within your department that you contact the Employee Labor and Relations Team prior to the recruitment process. This will expedite the recruitment process for you from the stage of submitting to posting. On your employee's last day Confirm that Supervisor and employee have reviewed steps on the Leaving Western webpage Confirm that the employee has returned all WWU property What to do in the event of an Employee Death Human Resources will coordinate EAP services based upon your needs. Communicate with your staff. Remember to provide self-care. What can HR do for you? Tips for Supporting Grieving Employees How to Listen to Someone Who is Hurting Make Waves. Human Resources 516 High Street, MS 9054 Bellingham, WA 98225-5996 360-650-3774 Fax: 360-650-2810 Visit Us Humanities Building 203 Please visit main HR webpage for office hours Closed Major Holidays Connect with Us General: HR@wwu.edu Benefits: HR.Benefits@wwu.edu Payroll: HR.Payroll@wwu.edu Medical Leave/Disability: HR.Disability@wwu.edu Footer Artwork Artwork by Gretchen Leggitt Tribal Lands Statement Western Washington University's main campus is situated on the ancestral homelands of the Coast Salish\n                    Peoples , who have lived in the Salish Sea basin, all throughout the San Juan Islands and the North Cascades\n                    watershed from time immemorial. We express our deepest respect and gratitude to our Indigenous neighbors,\n                    for their enduring care and protection of our shared lands and waterways. Western social media links Copyright and Contact Info Â© Western Washington University University Links and Policy Jobs Report Concerns Privacy Accessibility Notice Equal Employment Opportunity Policy"
    },
