      "title": "Locations",
      "description": "Work at Western | Western Washington University Skip to Content Home myWestern About About Western Our History Economic Impact Office of the President News Visit Locations Bellingham Peninsulas Everett Additional Sites Online Admissions and Aid First-Year Admissions Transfer Admissions Graduate Admissions International Admissions Orientation and Transition Tuition and Cost Financial Aid Scholarships Academics Majors and Programs Academic Advising & Student Achievement Center Colleges Libraries Institutes and Centers Summer Session Research Global Engagement Professional and Continuing Education University Catalog Life at Western Student Experience Housing and Dining Athletics Clubs, Organizations, and Events Accessibility, Diversity, Equity and Inclusion Counseling, Health, and Wellness Career Services International Student & Scholar Services Resource Directory Alumni & Foundation Athletics Parents & Families Menu Main navigation All Clear - Tue, 05/05/2026 - 08:44 Description Western Alert: Western is operating normally, and there are no alerts or advisories in effect. In the event of an emergency, call 911. Instruction Western Alert: Western is operating normally, and there are no alerts or advisories in effect. In the event of an emergency, call 911. Learn more about this alert Work at Western Searching for a Job? Looking to Hire? Desire to Volunteer? You're in the right place. Let's get you started. I am Seeking Employment Whether you are a student seeking work while you attend classes, a recent graduate looking for employment, or simply would like to work at Western - let us point you in the right direction. I want to work at Western I am a Western student I am a recent graduate I am an Employer Looking to hire an intern for the summer, or hire a student for a project? Or perhaps you need to hire a recent graduate with specific skills for a permanent full-time position? I want to hire Volunteer Opportunities If you're looking for volunteer opportunities, there are options on campus. In addition to the resources listed here, you can reach out to clubs, departments or other groups on campus to either find volunteers for your special event or to volunteer yourself! I want to volunteer I need a volunteer Seeking Employment? Whether you are a student seeking work while you attend classes, a recent graduate looking for employment, or simply would like to work at Western - let us point you in the right direction. I want to work at Western Ready to find work as staff or a faculty member at Western Washington University? Discover employment opportunities that could lead to your next career. Employment Opportunities at Western For questions about employment opportunities at Western, please reach out to hr@wwu.edu . I am a Western Student seeking... Career, Internship and/or Networking Opportunities. Career/Internship Job Listings Western's recruitment platform for careers and internships. Handshake is the #1 way college students find these opportunities. Help with my Career /Internship Search Discover resources and/or arrange to meet with someone who can help you. Employers Looking for the ideal candidate to hire? Start your search here. I want to hire for a... Summer, Part-time or Seasonal position I want to hire for part-time, seasonal or summer positions for students who are attending WWU or on summer break. Career and/or Internship Employment Opportunity I have an internship and/or a career related opportunity for a Western student/soon to be graduate that requires 0 – 3 years of experience. Volunteer Opportunities Connect to Volunteer and Service Learning Opportunities. Volunteering your time and expertise through nonprofit organizations can be a very gratifying experience. I Need a Volunteer Need a volunteer for a project? Connect with the W estern Action for Volunteer Engagement and Service, part of the Community Service Center, to get started. I'd Like to Volunteer on Campus Follow our registration process to be asked to volunteer by a department. Open to students and community members. Make Waves. Safety at Western Campus Safety Resources Title IX Sexual Harassment/Violence Emergency and Weather Information Western Policies Regarding Public Expression and Assembly Disclosure of Consumer Information WAC Docket Higher Education Emergency Relief Grant Reportage Business and Financial Resources Give to WWU Jobs Pay Bills Vendors Footer Artwork Artwork by Gretchen Leggitt Tribal Lands Statement Western Washington University's main campus is situated on the ancestral homelands of the Coast Salish\n                    Peoples , who have lived in the Salish Sea basin, all throughout the San Juan Islands and the North Cascades\n                    watershed from time immemorial. We express our deepest respect and gratitude to our Indigenous neighbors,\n                    for their enduring care and protection of our shared lands and waterways. Western social media links Copyright and Contact Info Â© Western Washington University University Links and Policy Jobs Report Concerns Privacy Accessibility Notice Equal Employment Opportunity Policy"
